From 8d37da32f4440fcb2efd866fe2659c75cfdf1238 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 19 Sep 2026 09:14:20 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 2/5] Close the write-path edge functions to the public

The anon key is a valid JWT and ships in the browser bundle, so verify_jwt
alone restricted nothing: any visitor could call these functions, and
scrape-ngo-feeds-cron and classify-articles had verify_jwt = false outright.

scrape-ngo-feeds was the serious one. It accepted a caller-supplied `ngos`
array including feedUrl, fetched those URLs, and filed the results under the
caller's chosen NGO name - letting an unauthenticated third party both reach
arbitrary URLs from the function and inject a fabricated dispatch signed by a
real organisation into the public feed.

- _shared/auth.ts: constant-time cron-secret check plus an admin/editor role
  check against the caller's own JWT. An unset CRON_SECRET denies rather than
  falls open.
- _shared/ngo-directory.ts: the 151 organisations now live server-side.
  Callers may only choose an offset/limit window into that list.
- Gate scrape-ngo-feeds, scrape-ngo-news, classify-articles, backfill-articles
  and the cron entry point; set verify_jwt = true everywhere as defence in depth.
- Hide the feed's Refresh button from non-staff: each press spends Firecrawl
  and AI-gateway credits.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
